<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Penthièvre</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Penthièvre is a historic region of northern Brittany, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, around Lamballe and the bay of Saint-Brieuc. It became a county held by a branch of the ducal house of Brittany in the 11th century, and the claim of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-penthievre">Joan of Penthièvre</a> to the duchy led to the Breton War of Succession of 1341–1364. It later passed to French noble families and was raised to a duchy in 1569.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/penthievre.jpg" alt="Penthièvre" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: GwenofGwened · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banni%C3%A8re_Maison_Penthi%C3%A8vre.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
